        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "82816de8-1506-52de-9171-74d499f3cd40",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Cepello, Jesse Ventura, Mark Dayton, Steve Strong, \"Chicago\" Steve Barkley\n- Places: Minnesota, Governor's Mansion, Minnesota State Capitol, Monterey\n- Roles: Governor of Minnesota, wrestler, artist, comedian\n- Works: Elephant Parts, music videos, portraits\n- Organizations: Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party\n\nFacts:\n- After retiring from wrestling to focus on his art career, Stephen Cepello was selected to paint the official Governor's Mansion and Minnesota State Capitol portraits of former wrestler and Governor of Minnesota Jesse Ventura.\n- \"Elephant Parts\" is a one-hour work with parody commercials, comedy sketches, and five full-length music videos.\n- \"Elephant Parts\" includes the popular songs \"Rio\" and \"Cruisin'.\"\n- The music video for \"Cruisin'\" featured wrestler Steve Strong and Monterey-based comic \"Chicago\" Steve Barkley.\n- The current Governor of Minnesota is Mark Dayton of the Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
